{"aggregate_id": "01M4TF9T1Y9FXSZZRK1DDBEYV6", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01M4TF9WR3PZQ4V993KBHXNT99", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"actor": "noreply@anthropic.com", "created_at": "2026-10-13T11:10:30.201185+00:00", "friendly_name": "Command-skill regeneration follow-ups (#6155)", "mission_id": "01M4TF9T1Y9FXSZZRK1DDBEYV6", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "command-skill-regen-followups-01M4TF9T", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "Three follow-ups deferred from the landing of PR #6113 (#702). The shared command-skill projection .agents/skills/spec-kitty.<command>/SKILL.md is a DERIVED, git-ignored surface (shared_skills_projection in src/specify_cli/state/contract.py) that #6113 began regenerating on drift. #6155 asks that: (1) each regenerated path is named once in human and --json output under surface_repair, without changing the exit code or outcome kind; (2) the regenerate branch reads shared_skills_projection from STATE_SURFACES at runtime and regenerates only while it is DERIVED and IGNORED, otherwise falling through to the existing consent branch; (3) _CommandBatch.remove_entry applies the same rule to prune a retired command's drifted, manifest-owned projection and its manifest entry, still refusing a directory and never touching an unowned path.", "purpose_tldr": "init/upgrade/agent config sync name regenerated command skills, read the DERIVED/IGNORED surface class from the state contract at runtime, and prune a retired command's drifted projection", "target_branch": "issue-6155-command-skill-regeneration-followups", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "spec-kitty", "project_uuid": "8a4a7da6-a97c-4bb4-893a-b31664abfee4", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-10-13T11:10:30.659721+00:00"}
